==Strategy==
A round of applause please for Inumusha finally making his first appearance in Zero Legends! This time he's accompanied by Winged Pigge, Tarsiriel and 2 Bore Jrs. Lure Tarsiriel near your base while sending out send out an occasional [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling]] to ward off Inumusha, then jump Tarsiriel with [[Talents|Talented]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] to get rid of it ASAP. Then, push Inumusha all the way back to the Doge Base with [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cats]] and [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cats]] and keep him stunlocked there. Be sure to have a consistent flow of [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cats]] so the Doge Base doesn't instantly kill everything. The first Bore Jr. isn't accompanied by anything dangerous, so he's easy enough to take care of. Once Winged Pigge shows up, stop stalling, lure her to the Cat Base, then use [[Master of Logic Newtone (Special Cat)|Master of Logic Newtone]] and [[Phantom Cat (Rare Cat)|Bubble Cat]] to quickly whittle her down. Holy Blast Inumusha whenever you can, it forces him to consistently play catchup, preventing him from supporting Winged Pigge. The second bore Jr. will be more of an issue; when he appears, get ready to burst it down with Awakened Bahamut Cat who will be off cooldown by this point. If you fail the timing, use Newtone's Conjure to get him extremely low, then finish him off with [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]]. Afterwards, you free to kill Winged Pigge, before then returning Ryan Gosling back to his grave of irrelevancy.

==Trivia==
*Bowl of Bliss's Japanese name, Ippai no Shiawase (一杯の幸せ, "Containerful of Happiness"; 一杯 can mean a bowlful, cupful, spoonful, etc.), may be a reference to ''[[wikipedia:ja:スプーン一杯の幸せ|Spoon Ippai no Shiawase]]'' (スプーン一杯の幸せ, "Spoonful of Happiness"), a series of novels by [[wikipedia:Keiko Ochiai|Keiko Ochiai]] that was adapted into a film starring [[wikipedia:Junko Sakurada|Junko Sakurada]]. ''Spoon Ippai no Shiawase'' is also the name of Sakurada's [[wikia:jpop:Spoon Ippai no Shiawase|fourth album]], which includes the film's theme song, "Hitori Aruki".

